# Project Root vs AI Coding Separation

Purpose:
  Keep human code and AI execution context separate.

Structure:
  project/                 # Human code root
    backend/
    frontend/
    database/
    tests/
    docs/                  # Human-readable docs
      index.md

  .sdd/                     # AI context root
    PROJECT.sdd             # Project intent
    project/                # AI project model (schemas, structure rules)
      PROJECT.sdd
      domains.sdd
      modules.sdd
      map.sdd
      flows.sdd
      dependencies.sdd
      indexes.sdd
      instantiation.sdd
      mode.sdd
      architecture.sdd
    projects/               # Concrete project instances
      vkard.az/
        INDEX.sdd
        decisions/
        tasks/
        docs/
        stack/
        context/
        cases/
        bugs/
        dependencies/
        gates/
        observability/
        workflow/
        architecture/
        testing/
        tokens/
    chains/                 # Execution chains
      graph.sdd
      default.sdd
      arms/
      rules/
      tokens/
    skills/                 # Skill catalog
    prompts/                # Prompt templates
    workflows/              # Workflow definitions
    state/                  # State notation

Rules:
  [S1] AI MUST start from .sdd/, never from project/ directly.
  [S2] AI MUST read .sdd/instances/vkard.az/docs/ before touching project/.
  [S3] AI MUST get human approval before writing to project/.
  [S4] project/ is the source of truth for code.
  [S5] .sdd/ is the source of truth for intent.
  [S6] docs/ under project/ is human language.
  [S7] .sdd/project/ is AI language (model schemas only).

Context Flow:
  prompt
    -> .sdd/chains/arms/prompt.sdd (P1)
    -> .sdd/instances/vkard.az/docs/ (human docs)
    -> human approval
    -> .sdd/project/ (AI model)
    -> .sdd/chains/arms/code.sdd (C1)
     -> project/ (human code)

State: +
